# NOBORU LEARNING ARCHITECTURE RULE

Version: 1.0

Priority: CRITICAL

Status: AUTHORITATIVE

This rule governs learning progression orchestration across Noboru.

Every learning-related system must follow docs/NOBORU LEARNING ARCHITECTURE BIBLE.md and import shared rules from lib/learning/.

docs/jlpt-content-architecture.md remains authoritative for curriculum structure (what content exists per JLPT level).

This bible and lib/learning/ are authoritative for runtime pedagogy (how content is introduced, mixed, reviewed, and gated).

⸻

PURPOSE

Ensure long-term retention over speed.

Every piece of content must help the player remember and use Japanese six months from now.

⸻

REQUIREMENTS

Shared Implementation

* Import constants, validators, and mixers from lib/learning/ — never duplicate bible values inline
* Golden Content Rule: validate at service boundaries via validateGoldenContentRule or assertGoldenContentRule
* Active Vocabulary Pool: use buildActiveVocabularyPool for stories, quests, companion, games, and AI context
* Session mix: use mixSessionItems / computeSessionMixCounts for ~70% review / 30% new
* Vocabulary intro limits: enforce VOCAB_INTRO_LIMITS_BY_JLPT when assembling mini chapters
* Mastery: evaluateWordMastery for bible depth requirements; SRS state maps via mapReviewStateToLifecycleStage
* Review intervals: REVIEW_INTERVAL_DAYS from lib/learning/ is canonical

World Tree Mapping (until branch schema exists)

* region → JLPT level
* unit → branch (thematic)
* lesson → mini chapter
* practice lesson → checkpoint
* trial → boss examination

See WORLD_TREE_CMS_ALIASES in lib/learning/learning-architecture.constants.ts.

AI Content

* All AI generation must receive PlayerKnowledgeContext
* AI may only use known/mastered vocabulary and unlocked grammar
* Application must function without AI

Feature Boundaries

* vocabulary owns word data and per-word progress persistence
* review owns SRS scheduling and due queues
* learning owns lesson assembly and path orchestration
* lib/learning owns cross-feature pedagogy rules

⸻

FORBIDDEN

* Introducing vocabulary in stories, quests, or exams without prior introduction (golden rule)
* Increasing difficulty via random unknown vocabulary
* Hardcoding bible constants outside lib/learning/
* Skipping review mix for progression-only sessions labeled as learning
* Treating single correct answers as mastery

⸻

REFERENCES

* docs/NOBORU LEARNING ARCHITECTURE BIBLE.md — full specification
* lib/learning/ — canonical implementation
* docs/jlpt-content-architecture.md — curriculum structure
* docs/world-map-learning-journey-system.md — journey UI and gating

